Allow the HTTP resolve endpoint to be served on multiple paths.

The upstream server registers exactly one HTTP path on its ServeMux, so the
DoH endpoint is only reachable under a single URL.  This patch splits the
"path" configuration option on commas and registers every part, which makes it
possible to serve the endpoint on the RFC 8484 standard path (/dns-query) as
well as on the legacy path (/getnsrecord) at the same time.

The patch is applied by the Docker build.  The build fails when the patch does
not apply, so an upstream release that changed this code will not silently
produce an image with a single path.

--- a/doh-server/server.go
+++ b/doh-server/server.go
@@ -101,7 +101,10 @@
 			LocalAddr: tcpLocalAddr,
 		}
 	}
-	s.servemux.HandleFunc(conf.Path, s.handlerFunc)
+	// Multiple paths can be configured as a comma separated list.
+	for _, path := range strings.Split(conf.Path, ",") {
+		s.servemux.HandleFunc(path, s.handlerFunc)
+	}
 	return s, nil
 }

